My Priest just reached Orcus Town, made his way over to Orcus, and
started fighting.  As I made my way back towards the upstairs, Orcus
called in a friend: Demogorgon.

At this point I made a terrible, terrible blunder: I flashed
Demogorgon with my expensive camera.  Then I engraved Elbereth and
wondered why the hell he was still pounding me, until comprehension
dawned and I uttered a groan of purest dismay.

At this point I should have dug down to the next level at the first
opportunity, but I compounded my error by continuing to trek back
towards the upstairs.  Demogorgon and Orcus teleport-tag-teamed me,
but I was always able to take care of the illness with a cure sickness
spell.  Although I'd dug a straight path back to the stairs, summoned
nasties forced me to detour a few times.

By the time I reached the stairs, which Demogorgon was squatting on,
I'd used all my mana on curing sickness, including a recharge from the
Mitre, and quaffed all three of my reserve potions of full healing.
Demogorgon was still blind (according to my stethoscope) and still
stinging the shit out of me, often twice per turn.  At this point it
occurred to me to check how long the blindness from a camera lasts:
1d50 turns.  WTF?  A straight walk from the downstairs to the upstairs
would have taken more than fifty turns, and I had taken much longer
than that.  How, how, how could Demogorgon still be blind?  Anyone
have any idea?

Another strange thing happened during this fight.  I engraved Elbereth
with a wand of fire.  Although Demogorgon ignored it, some other
monsters ran away, but they came back and attacked me again.  I
checked my square, and the engraving was gone.  "What the hell?" I
thought.  I engraved it again, and the monsters ran away again, but
came back and attacked again.  I checked the square again, and the
engraving was still there, but really messed up; like "f&k   ||" or
something.  How could this have happened when I used a supposedly-
permanent wand of fire?


